  "method": {
    "clips": "v004's level-2 composite at 100 m (EPSG:4326), each country's box snapped outward to its grid, cells unchanged except that every cell of a 256 × 256-cell tile whose box doesn't intersect the country's Natural Earth 1:50m outline is set to nodata; cloud-optimized GeoTIFF (DEFLATE level 9, no predictor, 256 px blocks, nearest-neighbour overviews); habitat_clips.parquet holds the same cells as PostGIS raster WKB, one row per tile holding a class cell (tiles numbered row-major from the upper left)",
    "countries": "method 3 (003 §5): v004's 1 km level-2 fractions (EPSG:4326, 0.009915667822884942° cells); per country, Σ fraction ÷ 1000 × the cell's geodesic area (WGS84) over the cells whose centre is inside its Natural Earth 1:50m outline (overlapping outlines both count a shared cell); partition classes only (open-water overlay 901, 1000, 1001, 1002, 1003, 1004 left out); km² rounded to 0.01; estimated from a map, not measured",
    "records": "the record's 1 km cell: the partition class with the largest fraction, ties to the lowest code; NULL when the cell holds none; the map's class at that place, not the species' habitat"
  },
